    <briefdescription>
<para>The hoop terms of the weak form of an axisymmetric particle, shared by its formulations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The increment of the hoop stretch is <formula id="29">$ \Delta F_{\theta\theta} = x_r / r = 1 + \Delta u_r / \bar r $</formula> at the particle center, with the radial displacement increment <formula id="30">$ \Delta u_r = N_B\, \Delta q_{Br} $</formula> there and its radius <formula id="15">$ \bar r $</formula> in the intermediate configuration. The virtual hoop strain is  <formula id="31">$ \delta d_{\theta\theta}
= \delta x_r / x_r = \delta u_r / (\bar r\, \Delta F_{\theta\theta}) $</formula>, so that the virtual work of the hoop stress over the undeformed ring, <formula id="32">$ \tau_{\theta\theta}\, \delta d_{\theta\theta}\, V_0 $</formula>, adds to the radial residual of node <formula id="33">$ A $</formula> the term <formula id="34">$ T_A\, \tau_{\theta\theta} / (\bar r\, \Delta F_{\theta\theta})\, V_0 $</formula>, with the test function <formula id="35">$ T_A $</formula> of the node at the center: the term <formula id="36">$ T_A / \bar r $</formula> is the hoop operator <formula id="20">$ \tilde H_A = N_A(\bar{\boldsymbol{Y}}) / \bar r $</formula> of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle_section_integrals" kindref="compound">ParticleSectionIntegrals</ref> with the test function (see there for why it is the point value). The faces of a particle carry the ring of their points (<ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_hoop_1a2c3bba2015b259961062d36733b18c00" kindref="member">ringOfFacePoint()</ref>). The derivation is on the page &quot;Axisymmetric Particles&quot; of the documentation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
